&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;The students,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;Eva (Grade 7) and&amp;nbsp;Neilliy&amp;nbsp;(Grade 8),&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;were last seen at the basketball game around 5 p.m. Once school officials realized the girls were missing, they&amp;nbsp;immediately&amp;nbsp;notified local authorities and the students&rsquo; families.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family:arial,arial_embeddedfont,arial_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

